Engine mingw: disable inline_asm_nonlocal_labels, as upstream's own guard for
clang + LTO + Windows does (llvm/llvm-project#76046). That guard sits under
`enabled lto`, i.e. ffmpeg's --enable-lto; here -flto comes from the stdenv,
so the probe passes and mlpdsp_init.c takes the address of labels defined
inside an asm block. COFF routes the reference through a .refptr COMDAT that
needs a global symbol, so all 14 ff_mlp_*order_* end up undefined at the link.
--enable-lto would reach the guard too, but also flips
inline_asm_direct_symbol_refs and symver_asm_label on every target.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -6532,7 +6532,7 @@
 
 check_inline_asm inline_asm_labels '"1:\n"'
 
-check_inline_asm inline_asm_nonlocal_labels '"Label:\n"'
+disable inline_asm_nonlocal_labels
 
 if enabled aarch64; then
     as_arch_level="armv8-a"
